WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.310
- Hey everybody, it's Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.160
So everybody who listens to the podcast,

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.470
I've been wanting to do this
concept for a long time.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.740
I did a version of it not too long ago.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.650
A couple episodes of the Brown Paper Bags

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.930
where we drink wine, but
these three wonderful people

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.070
are not gonna get served free alcohol.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:17.903
- Bye.

00:00:17.903 --> 00:00:19.630
- Yeah, I know, sorry, you're out?

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:20.463
You were promised something

00:00:20.463 --> 00:00:21.296
totally different, right?
- It's so nice.

00:00:21.296 --> 00:00:22.240
Thank you so much.
- You're out.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.290
I've always been
fascinated by what happens

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.310
when you bring different people together

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.920
that are doing interesting things

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.000
and just shoot the shit about what's going

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.660
on in culture, in the game.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.690
And I think a lot of people are,

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.170
in this group specifically,
I think from what I know

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.010
about them from afar, have crossovers

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.910
and see certain things the same way

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.330
and then obviously have
their unique journeys

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.460
and points of view.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.630
So I've been wanting to do--

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.160
There's this thing that I used to do

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.940
when I was first coming up
in the game in Silicon Valley

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.080
where I met all the hardcore Facebook

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.910
and Twitter founders and Uber founders.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.840
And they were called jam sessions

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.290
where we would get together
at these conferences

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.770
at like midnight in a hotel room

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:05.750
and for three, four hours just
talk about the game, right?

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.990
If we would have one tonight,

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:10.470
we would talk about
cryptocurrency, for sure.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.530
We did four years ago.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.730
That's why I bought
Bitcoin four years ago.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.220
So you just get different
ideas and thoughts about--

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.150
We would argue about who's
gonna be big, who's not.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.810
And so, I've been wanting to do this thing

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:24.430
called #podSessions, podcast
versions of the jam sessions,

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.350
and I'm very excited.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:27.540
I have three phenomenal guests

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.380
and probably one of the biggest things

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.540
that I wanna get out of
#podSessions is also an opportunity

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.170
for me as my career
changes to use my platform

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:39.120
of the attention that I'm
amassing to put other people

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.420
on that also sometimes have
bigger audiences than me,

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.140
different audiences
than me, or are emerging

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.410
and are doing interesting
things that have caught my eye,

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.340
normally through some digital connection

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.180
or the eye of somebody on my
team's digital connection.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.700
So that's what we're doing.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.150
I'm super excited about it.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.610
You guys are the three that
are helping me pop the cherry

00:01:58.610 --> 00:01:59.620
of #podSessions.
- Love it.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:00.990
Thank you.
- So thank you for being here.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.610
And so, why don't we introduce ourselves.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.630
